1008| ### 4.3 Model boundaries
1013| - The model does not check blade integrity. The blade root factor of safety sits at infinity in the model. The team deferred the full beam-on-supports blade model (PRD 0006:147). The rotor blades are not yet structurally gated in this analysis.
1031| ## 5 Conclusion
1033| The report screened 930 rigid-wing ground-generation rotary kite turbine designs with a tensile rotary power transmission (NR-001).
1034| The campaign scored each design on the ODE path over the measurement window (NR-015).
1035| One fixed power-law generator load and one fixed gate set held for every design (NR-015).
1037| The search found 508 feasible candidates in the searched space (NR-002).
1039| The 301 rejects split three ways (NR-055).
1040| 96 ran below the 5 kW power floor.
1041| Four ran at or above 5 kW with a factor of safety below 2.5.
1042| The remaining 201 carried no logged cause at campaign time. The re-run
1043| probe (NR-061) names them. 93 rotors fall below the power
1044| floor. 37 settle at the realisability cliff. 36 refuse on rotor spacing.
1045| 30 break a line. Three cross the Betz ceiling. Two diverge at the hub
